WEBVTT

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:35.980
<i>It's October, one month into the second term.</i>

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.990
<i>Fall's rushing closer, and...</i>

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.900
<i>Ta-da!</i>

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.990
<i>We're switching to our winter uniforms!</i>

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.680
My winter uniform's getting too small.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.060
You haven't even grown.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.860
I grew taller.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.200
No, you didn't.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.200
My breasts, too.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.630
They haven't changed.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.960
<i>Hinata's growth aside,</i>

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.640
<i>I'm going to work hard at school and in 
mountain climbing, with renewed enthusiasm.</i>

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.430
Morning!

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.640
Morning.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.340
Morning.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.780
<i>It's been a month since 
the second term started,</i>

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:19.610
<i>but I still don't have any friends 
in my class besides Hinata.</i>

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.870
<b>Having Fun with Classmates!</b>

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.870
<b>Hanno Forestry</b>

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.870
<b>Ship -> Edo</b>

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.870
<b>Edo Period</b>

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:29.720
And so, Hanno thrived on its forestry 
industry during the Edo period.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.380
They carried lumber to Edo by boat.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:36.960
<i>That variety show yesterday was fun.</i>

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.880
<i>I wonder if Hinata saw it.</i>

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.880
That's it for today.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.020
The Seibu game yesterday was amazing.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.900
He slid into home!

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.900
Safe! A come-from-behind victory!

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.760
Seibu saves it.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.940
What the heck?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.030
Hinata...

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.260
Are you into baseball, too, Hinata-chan?

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.260
Hinata...

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.640
Not really.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:01.580
Hina...

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.800
What's up, Aoi?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.480
Nothing! Not a thing!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.000
<b>Gloom</b>

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.790
<i>I was completely awkward.</i>

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.890
Say what?! Take that!

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.300
Hey, take it easy.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:27.170
<i>Kaede-san, Kokona-chan, 
Hikari-san, Honoka-chan...</i>

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:32.350
<i>I have more friends now, 
but I only have Hinata in class.</i>

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.830
<i>It doesn't matter, since she wasn't 
around during middle school,</i>

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.560
<i>but I guess it'd be nice if she were around.</i>

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:46.190
I lost track of how far I'd gotten.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.460
<i>It's not that I hate knitting on my own...</i>

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.750
<i>But chatting it up over 
nothing would be fun, too.</i>

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.000
Yukimura-san.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.630
What are you knitting? A scarf?

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.950
Yeah, a scyarf...

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.860
Er, a scarf.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.130
It's going to get colder soon.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.010
Is it for yourself?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.630
Yeah, for myself.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.730
You're so good.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.770
N-Not really.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.770
You are.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.700
You're always knitting something.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.550
I've always been amazed by how good you are.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.910
I'm pretty bad with my fingers.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.940
I tried to do spool knitting a 
long time ago and gave up.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.240
Oh...

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.810
You were knitting mittens 
the other day, weren't you?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.170
Y-Yeah.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.260
Those were for my mom.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:37.070
Before that, you were doing a coaster.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.750
Yeah, that one was, uh...

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.540
I gave it to Hikari-san.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.260
Hikari-san's my senpai at my work.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.940
You work at Susuki, right?

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.390
How did you know?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.480
I saw you when I passed 
by the shopping district.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.140
I buy cakes and stuff there sometimes.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.590
Oh, really?

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:57.080
When did you start?

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.120
At work.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.900
I started during summer break.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.120
Buying stuff for mountain 
climbing costs money, you know?

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.570
Oh, I do mountain climbing.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.030
With Hinata-chan, right?

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.140
Yeah, we go all over the place.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.160
Like where?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.660
Like Mitsutouge.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.940
Mitsutouge?

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.000
It has a great view of Mt. Fuji.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.040
Oh, I went to Mt. Fuji, too.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.060
Also, Mt. Tanigawa, and...

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.080
You're quite the outdoors type, huh?

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.120
I'm surprised.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.300
Yeah, I'm surprised, too, actually.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:28.550
Oh, come on.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:31.060
So I have to buy hiking equipment...

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.660
<i>Aoi's grown a bit.</i>

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.940
<i>Must be because of the mountain climbing.</i>

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.310
So you have the day off at work today, huh?

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:42.100
Yeah.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.380
Let's go hang out after school, then!

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.280
Okay.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.660
Sweet!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.120
U-Um...

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.710
Can Hinata come along?

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:56.910
Of course.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:02.720
What's wrong?

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.960
Yeah, so then...

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.310
No way!

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.500
I don't have confidence that 
I can be part of that group.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.060
Don't worry about it.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.560
You were talking just fine with Mio earlier.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.810
<b>Mio</b>

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.810
Kasumi and Yuri are just the same.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.810
<b>Kasumi</b>

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.810
<b>Yuri</b>

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.190
Just talk to them normally.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.150
It's the "normally" that I don't get.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.320
Weren't you in the same 
middle school as Kasumi?

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:25.320
Hey!

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:27.360
Hurry up!

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.940
We're coming!

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:32.680
Hey, at least you can hang 
out with other people now.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.510
You've grown.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:37.020
Why are you so condescending?

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.410
Relax, relax.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.080
<b>Karaoke</b>

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.350
I'll stuff all my mistakes

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:51.200
Tightly into my seat pocket

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:56.630
And use them as my power 
to take the next step

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:57.900
<i>What do I do now?</i>

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:01.140
<i>I've never been in a karaoke box before.</i>

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:01.780
Hurry over here

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:05.730
I can't help turning to look

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:09.240
Before I know it, I'm smiling

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.400
<i>Sh-She's good!</i>

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:16.250
The scenery I wanted to see...

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.250
<i>She's so good!</i>

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.380
Whether it's sunny or rainy...

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.690
<i>They're all so good.</i>

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.630
<i>Wh-What should I do?</i>

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.160
<i>Hinata's next?</i>

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.210
<i>That means...</i>

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.550
<i>I'll be next!</i>

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.560
<i>Wh-What do I do?</i>

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.850
<i>Is there any way I can avoid singing?</i>

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.320
<i>I know. I could go to the restroom.</i>

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.070
Here.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.230
You should queue a song, too, Aoi.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.860
<i>She just cut off my escape route!</i>

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.620
<i>I hate you, Hinata.</i>

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.410
<b>New Songs | By Artist | By Title</b>

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.580
<i>Um, let's see...</i>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.660
<b>Starting with "A"</b>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.660
<b>For Love</b>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.660
<b>Dash to the Red Sunset</b>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.660
<b>Jet Star Union</b>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.660
<b>Un Deux Trois</b>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.660
<b>Amechans</b>

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.660
<b>Pray to Andromeda</b>

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.360
<i>Which song do I know?</i>

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.540
<b>Girl & Girl & Boy</b>

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.540
<b>Mountaineer's Song</b>

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.540
<b>Carrying On at the Edge</b>

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.540
<i>I know this song.</i>

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.290
<i>I can sing this!</i>

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.400
<i>Wait a second...</i>

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.300
<i>But...</i>

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:13.090
The call of shooting stars...

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:17.390
At the glissades...

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.440
What is this song?

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.440
Dunno.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.180
It's super obscure.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:28.030
<i>What do I do if that happens?</i>

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.030
<b>Mountaineer's Song</b>

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.030
<b>Lyrics/Music: Unknown</b>

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.030
Oh, that's me.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.280
<i>That song's so obscure, Hinata!</i>

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:42.590
The call of shooting stars...

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:47.040
At the glissades...

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:56.620
Will I find that person, 
holding a flower in their mouth?

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:56.840
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:06.230
It's the love song of the Alps

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.430
<i>Everyone's actually listening.</i>

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:16.240
The mountaineer from way back...

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.940
<i>Hinata's having fun, too.</i>

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:22.130
<i>Maybe I don't need to overthink things.</i>

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:27.700
<i>Oh, I can sing this one.</i>

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:28.790
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:29.880
<b>Queue</b>

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:29.880
<i>Go!</i>

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.330
I've never heard that song before.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.560
Right?

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.090
So, what's the next song?

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.970
<b>Summer-Colored Gifts</b>

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.970
<b>Lyrics: Inaba Emi</b>

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.970
<b>Music:</b>

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.740
Whose song is this?

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:50.100
When we make it through 
together is the best gift

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:55.380
It's my heart's greatest treasure

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.260
I know this song.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.520
Can I sing with you?

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:01.700
Y-Yeah.

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:09.960
If I make a square with my fingers

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:17.340
Maybe I can cut out the scenery in front of me

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.650
Relax.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:23.470
This day will never come back

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:30.480
The blue of the sky, our awestruck 
faces, and our shared smiles

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:38.030
They're our matching gifts, the precious days 
we spent laughing and crying together

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:44.510
Ten years later, a hundred years later, 
the memories won't have faded

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.450
I'll still be holding half of it

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:04.390
Summer-colored gifts!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.690
<b>Karaoke</b>

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.510
We sang so much.

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:16.460
My throat's killing me.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:17.940
It's not <i>that</i> bad.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:22.450
<i>I kind of had fun.</i>

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.580
<i>Maybe I'm fitting in a bit.</i>

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:26.820
Aoi-chan.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.020
Y-Yes?

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.450
Where should we go next?

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:32.310
Wh-Where do you usually go?

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:35.720
Well, there's Tokorozawa, Kotezashi...

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.210
Or Ikebukuro.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.340
Huh.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.440
Wh-What?

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:43.940
Nothing.

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:45.830
What? Jeez.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.990
<i>Hinata looks so smug.</i>

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:53.060
<i>But I don't think I could have sung 
as well if I'd come by myself.</i>

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:55.740
<i>I guess I should be a little grateful.</i>

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:57.190
Thanks.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.940
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:59.240
To be continued.
